mothershipOS: while the device can't be opened (the external display's audio before the monitor is lit, or while
it is unplugged), run the guest's stream on ALSA "null" with the same parameters instead of failing: a guest
that sees prepare fail writes the device off (PipeWire falls back to a dummy output, seen at every VM start, as
the guest probes its card a few seconds before the monitor is lit). prepare() reopens the device on every
playback start, so the sound comes once the device is up.

